@deanwball When I was one of the early bloggers at Microsoft, I went through this myself. Being associated with a big organization changes how people perceive you and work with you, both pro and con. 

On my first week at Microsoft, my boss Jeff Sandquist told me, "Beware of the royal we." He told me everyone will answer your phone calls because it's Microsoft calling, not Robert Scoble.

Good luck figuring it out. Yep, it does change you, but it gives you superpowers too, which you haven't really explored here yet.

